   "evidence": "Induction.lean:89 `@[simp] theorem indK0_of`; :125 `@[simp high + 1] theorem indK0_of_trivial`; :153 `@[simp high] theorem indK0_of_indFDRep`; same ladder in Restriction.lean:77/106/135 (`resK0_of` / `resK0_of_asModule` / `resK0_of_trivial`). Induction.lean:138 has no attribute, and unlike `indOfMulActionQuotientEquiv_apply_mk` (Permutation.lean:318, where a comment justifies omitting `simp`) no reason is given.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/GrothendieckGroup/GroupAlgebra/Induction.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp high]` (matching `indK0_of_indFDRep`, or `high + 1` as on `indK0_of_trivial`). No loop risk: the RHS contains no `indK0`, the pattern `Subgroup.subgroupOf ?D S` is distinct from the `Representation.trivial` LHS, and the side goal `D \u2264 S` simply fails to discharge when absent, falling through to `indK0_of`.",
   "issue": "`indK0_of_ofMulAction_quotient` is unannotated, while the generic `indK0_of` is `@[simp]` and matches the same LHS `indK0 k S (ExactK0.of (FGModuleCat.of k[S] _))`. `simp` on a goal containing `indK0 k S [k[S \u29f8 D.subgroupOf S]]` therefore normalizes to the `finiteModulesCoextendScalars` Hom-module, discarding the identification this PR proves.",
   "line": "138"
  }
 ],
